// SVG 2 (https://svgwg.org/svg2-draft/) uses SVGRect, SVGMatrix and SVGPoint
// as types - SVGGraphicsElement.getBBox(), getCTM(), SVGAnimatedRect,
// SVGPointList, SVGSVGElement.createSVGRect() and the rest - and webref's
// SVG.idl (so also WPT's interfaces/SVG.idl) has them so. Those names are
// only the [LegacyWindowAlias]es of DOMRect, DOMMatrix and DOMPoint in
// Geometry Interfaces 1 (https://drafts.csswg.org/geometry-1/, geometry.idl),
// and WebIDL does not make a legacy window alias a type name, so codegen
// would bind the members as untyped values.
//
// These typedefs give codegen the type the browsers bind: getBBox() returns
// a DOMRect in Chrome, Firefox and Safari, and window.SVGRect === DOMRect.
// A typedef creates no global; the window aliases stay geometry.idl's.

typedef DOMRect SVGRect;
typedef DOMMatrix SVGMatrix;
typedef DOMPoint SVGPoint;
